App_as_Code_001

Automated Application Deployment and Configuration
As a Product Engineer / Platform Engineer,
I want application deployments and configuration to be automated and repeatable across environments,
so that reliance on manual activities is reduced, the risk of misconfiguration is lowered, and services can be delivered securely and at pace.

 

.

Scenario: Deployments and configuration are automated

Given an application is ready to be deployed

When deployment and configuration are executed

Then they are performed automatically without manual steps

And manual intervention is not required to complete a successful deployment.

Scenario: Deployments are repeatable across environments

Given the same application version is deployed to different environments

When the deployment process is repeated

Then deployments produce consistent and predictable outcomes

And configuration does not vary due to manual actions.

 

 

 

 

 

 

App_as_Code_002

Configuration Drift Control
As a Product Team,
We want the organisation to continuously detect and automatically remediate unauthorised or unsupported configuration changes across in-scope applications, middleware and databases, 
So that systems remain aligned to approved secure baselines, vulnerability exposure is minimised, and operational or audit risk does not accumulate between deployments and patch cycles.

Scenario: Detect unauthorised changes

Given manual changes can be applied outside of the application deployment pipeline

When scheduled scans or continuous checks run

Then live configurations must be compared against the version stored in the repository. 

 

Scenario: Remediate unauthorised changes

Given a manual change has been applied

When scheduled scans or continuous checks are ran 

Then configuration is updated to match the version stored in the repository

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

App_as_Code_003

Automated Security Hardening and Patching (middleware and database)
As a Cyber Security Engineer,

I want the system to automatically apply and validate approved security hardening and patches,

So that we minimize our vulnerability window and ensure continuous audit compliance without manual intervention.

Scenario: Automatically apply approved security hardening and patches

Given middleware or database components are deployed, updated, or identified as requiring security remediation

When automated security controls are executed

Then approved security hardening controls and security patches are applied automatically

 

Scenario: Security hardening and patches are validated after application

Given security hardening controls and patches have been applied

When validation is performed

Then the system confirms that the required controls and patches are correctly applied

And any failure, partial application, or non‑compliance is detected and recorded


 

 

 

 

 

App_as_Code_004

Evidence‑Driven Configuration Assurance
As a Cyber Security Engineer,
I want clear, auditable evidence that deployed configurations and patch levels continuously follow approved standards,
so that cyber assurance is maintained, regulatory compliance can be demonstrated, and audits or security incidents can be responded to quickly and effectively.

Scenario: Continuous Configuration Compliance Monitoring

Given an approved configuration and patch baseline exists

When systems are deployed or updated in the environment

Then the system must automatically assess and record whether configurations and patch levels align with the approved baseline

 

Scenario: Evidence Generation and Storage

Given configuration and patch compliance checks are performed

When results are generated

Then the system must store auditable evidence including timestamps, system identifiers, baseline references, and compliance status

 

Scenario: Audit Reporting

Given an auditor requests evidence of configuration and patch compliance

When a report is generated

Then the system must provide clear, exportable reports showing historical and current compliance status across systems

 

Scenario: Integrity and Auditability of Evidence

Given compliance evidence is stored

When it is accessed or reviewed

Then the evidence must be tamper‑evident and maintain a complete audit trail of changes and access 

 

 

 

 

 

App_as_Code_005

Reduction of Manual Controls and Rework
As a Product Engineer,
I want configuration checks, setup activities, and post‑deployment changes to be performed automatically and consistently,
so that reliance on manual intervention is reduced, configuration‑related incidents are minimised, and engineering teams can focus on delivering value rather than rework.

Scenario: Elimination of Manual Verification Steps

Given a deployment pipeline exists

When a release progresses through environments

Then all configuration and security checks must be executed automatically within the pipeline, removing manual approval or verification steps wherever possible

 

Scenario: Reduction of Post‑Deployment Fixes

Given a deployment has completed

When the system enters operational use

Then there must be no requirement for manual configuration fixes due to missed or inconsistent setup activities

 

Scenario: Security Risk Reduction through Automation

Given manual configuration activities are identified as a source of risk

When automation policies are implemented

Then the number of configuration‑related security incidents must be reduced through consistent, repeatable automated controls

 

Scenario: Auditability of Automated Controls

Given automated processes replace manual controls

When configuration actions and validations occur

Then the system must produce auditable logs demonstrating that controls were executed consistently and successfully

 

Scenario: Engineering Productivity Improvement

Given engineering teams perform deployments and configuration tasks

When automation is in place

Then the time spent on manual setup, validation, and rework must be reduced, enabling focus on higher‑value engineering and security improvements

 

 

 

 

 

App_as_Code_006

Configuration and Health Monitoring
As a Cyber Security Operations Analyst / Platform Engineer,
I want continuous monitoring and validation of the health and baseline configuration compliance of application platforms, middleware, runtime environments, and databases (excluding custom application code),
So that I can detect security or stability issues early and support faster, evidence‑driven recovery during incidents.

Scenario: Continuous Platform Health Monitoring

Given application platforms, middleware, runtime environments, and databases are deployed

When systems are in operation

Then their baseline health (availability, performance, resource utilisation, and error conditions) must be continuously monitored

 

Scenario: Exclusion of Custom Application Code

Given application workloads include custom-developed code

When monitoring and validation are performed

Then only platform, middleware, runtime, and database layers are assessed, explicitly excluding custom application code

 

Scenario: Evidence and Audit Logging

Given monitoring and validation activities occur

When results are generated

Then logs must be retained with timestamps, system identifiers, and compliance/health status to support audit and forensic needs

 

 

 

 

 

App_as_Code_007

Scalable and Governed Delivery Capability
As an App Owner,
I want to use a centralised library of governed CI/CD templates with embedded security controls,
So that I can deploy applications consistently and securely at scale without manual security reconfiguration.

Scenario: Standardised Deployment using a Governed Template

Given a developer is onboarding a new application to the platform

And a library of approved, hardened deployment templates exists

When the developer references the governed template in their pipeline configuration

Then the application is deployed using the organization's standard security configurations

And all mandatory cyber controls (e.g., secret scanning, image signing) are automatically executed.

 

Scenario: Detection of Non-Compliant Configuration

Given an application is using a governed deployment template

When a user attempts to override a mandatory security control (e.g., disabling port 443 requirement)

Then the deployment pipeline must fail

And an error message must be returned stating that the configuration violates organizational security policy.

 

 

 

 

 

App_as_Code_008

Deployment Guardrails & Runtime Compliance
As a Product Team,

we want the CI/CD pipeline to automatically verify application, middleware and database versions against the approved runtime compatibility and security baseline,

so that only supported, secure, and compliant technology stacks can be deployed into any environment.

Scenario: Automatically verify against security baseline

Given a deployment is initiated through the CI/CD pipeline

When the pipeline validates the deployment contents

Then all runtime technologies and versions are checked against the approved Runtime Technology Compatibility Matrix

And validation occurs before any installation takes place

Scenario: Unsupported runtime stacks are automatically blocked

Given unapproved runtimes have been detected

When deployment is initiated

Then guardrails prevent deployment of unapproved/non-compliant technology stacks

Scenario: Provide  clear audit trail of approved and rejected deployments

Given a deployment is validated by the CI/CD pipeline

When a validation decision is reached (approved or rejected)

Then the decision is automatically logged for every validation without exception

And the log records whether the deployment was approved or rejected

And where rejected, the reason for rejection is captured

And sufficient detail is recorded to identify the deployment

And the logged information provides a clear, retrievable audit trail of validation decisions over time

 

 

 

 

 
